From 31868aa3ad7816fbb9a1a478da4b4cea69881287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:16:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0/2] drm/amdgpu, drm/radeon: Prefer exact bus match for VFCT images

The VFCT soft filter added in commits 11c141672045 and 4059e2f02c8a
takes the first VFCT image whose vendor, device, slot and function
match, even when a later image also matches the bus number.  On
systems with several identical GPUs every GPU then gets the first GPU's
image.  This came up during review of the soft filter ("how they would
interplay with a system with multiple of the same GPU") and Alex pointed
out that some Apple systems do exactly that.  The Mac Pro 6,1 is one:

  02:00.0 1002:6798 113-C3861XA-028
  06:00.0 1002:6798 113-C3861XB-028

These patches scan the whole table and prefer the image with an exact bus
match, falling back to the first identity match only when no bus number
matches, so the pci=realloc case the soft filter was added for still
works.

The fallback is still ambiguous when the buses of several identical GPUs
are renumbered: they all get the first image, as they do today.  Refusing
the VFCT image in that case would be stricter, but it could leave a GPU
with no VBIOS at all, so these patches leave that behaviour alone.

Testing, on a Mac Pro 6,1 (2x FirePro D700, Apple VFCT above):

- Replayed the machine's VFCT through the old and new
  amdgpu_acpi_vfct_bios() and radeon_acpi_vfct_bios() compiled in
  userspace.  With the old code the GPU at 06:00.0 gets
  113-C3861XA-028; with the new code it gets 113-C3861XB-028.  An
  exact-bus single-GPU table, a renumbered single-GPU table and a
  non-matching device ID behave the same as before.
- Booted the patches backported to 6.12.111 on the Mac Pro.  amdgpu
  fetched 113-C3861XA-028 for 02:00.0 and 113-C3861XB-028 for 06:00.0
  from VFCT with no bus mismatch notice, and both GPUs initialized.
  radeon initialized both GPUs with no VFCT warnings or bus mismatch
  notice.  radeon doesn't log which VBIOS source it used, but both
  drivers try ATRM before VFCT and amdgpu fell through to VFCT on this
  machine.
- Built both files with W=1, with and without CONFIG_ACPI.

Tom Fairfield (2):
  drm/amdgpu: Prefer exact bus match when picking a VFCT image
  drm/radeon: Prefer exact bus match when picking a VFCT image

